WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.720
Standardized protocols and volume manufacturing cut pager prices from hundreds of dollars to tens by the 1980s.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:16.780
This is First Principles Daily, episode 111. In the 1950s, a hospital pager was a low volume VHF radio built one at a time.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:25.340
Its price came from hand-tuned circuits and small batch crystals. By the 1980s, the same function reached the market for tens of dollars.

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:31.600
engineers stopped treating each unit as a custom receiver. They treated it instead as a standardized

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:37.140
one-way message device. The difference came from asking what the radio link actually required

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:43.660
at the level of frequency, modulation, and parts count. Early paging systems grew out of two-way

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:50.340
mobile radio practice. Manufacturers took the same VHF transmitters, receivers, and crystal-controlled

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:56.080
local oscillators already used in police and taxi fleets. They simply removed the transmitter

00:00:56.080 --> 00:01:01.520
from the portable unit. That decision locked in a parts list built around individually selected

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:07.900
crystals, discrete tune circuits, and metal housings. Each hospital or city ordered only a few

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:13.400
dozen units. There was never enough volume to justify custom silicon or automated crystal

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:19.540
production lines. The resulting price reflected low utilization of test equipment, skilled alignment

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:25.200
labor and the need to stock many different crystal frequencies. Hospitals accepted the cost

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:30.680
because the alternative was a nurse walking the wards with paper messages. Each receiver still

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:36.240
carried a full super-heterodine front end with multiple IF stages and manual peaking adjustments.

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:42.440
Frequency stability depended on temperature compensated crystal ovens or hand-selected units pulled

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:48.360
from larger batches. The housing remained a machined or die-cast metal enclosure sized for the

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:49.540
two-way radio market.

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:55.040
Every new customer order restarted the same low-volume procurement and alignment cycle.

00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:59.600
The decisive step was to define the service as one-way digital messaging.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:05.500
Engineers then asked what minimum set of components could deliver a short numeric or alphanumeric

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:08.400
string to a receiver that woke only when addressed.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:14.640
POXIG supplied the answer by fixing a common data rate, modulation scheme, and addressing

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:17.220
format that every manufacturer could implement.

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:23.080
With the protocol frozen, the receiver no longer needed wide tuning range or continuous listening.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:29.260
It could use a single fixed frequency crystal and a simple decoder that powered down between message slots.

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:38.420
That change eliminated the variable capacitors, multiple crystal sockets, and continuous draw receiver stages that had dominated earlier designs.

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:45.880
High volume quartz crystal production drove the cost of the frequency reference from tens of dollars per unit down to a few dollars.

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:51.360
The same blank could be cut and plated for millions of identical pages rather than dozens

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:52.480
of different frequencies.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:57.780
Once the frequency reference was cheap and stable, designers could integrate the remaining

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:02.580
decoding and alerting functions into a single application-specific integrated circuit.

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:06.400
The ASIC replaced dozens of discrete logic packages.

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:11.880
Each of those packages had previously required separate procurement, placement, and soldering.

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:18.140
Because the protocol was public, multiple semi-conductor firms could amortize mask costs across

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:19.520
the same customer base.

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:22.900
Crystal cost fell with volume and standardization.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:25.260
Longick cost fell with integration.

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:28.480
Assembly cost fell with fewer packages to place.

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:34.820
The finished pager moved closer to the raw material floor set by silicon, quartz, a small battery,

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:35.960
and a plastic housing.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:41.300
A rough magic wand estimate starts with a few cents of high-purity quartz for the crystal

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:47.380
blank. It adds a few dollars of silicon wafer area for the decoder die. It adds pennies

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:51.840
for the molded plastic case and a comparable amount for the button cell battery chemistry.

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:57.900
Adding those commodity values yields a floor well below $10 even before assembly labor.

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:05.360
The original VHF unit sat at an idiot index of perhaps 30-50. Their finished price reflected

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:09.720
custom alignment and low-volume crystals rather than the material content itself.

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:16.340
Poxag removed the need for continuous receiver draw by defining precise time slots and address bits.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:20.880
The radio section could remain powered off for the great majority of each minute.

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:25.980
This duty cycling requirement allowed a simpler single-conversion receiver topology

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:31.850
instead of the multi-stage super-head chain. The fixed data rate also permitted the use of

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:35.670
inexpensive ceramic filters rather than tunable LC tanks.

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:41.330
As production volume rose into the millions, the same crystal blank could be frequency-trimmed

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:43.210
by laser rather than by hand.

00:04:43.810 --> 00:04:48.870
The ASIC absorbed the address comparator, error correction logic, and alert driver that

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:52.630
had previously lived in separate TTL or CMS packages.

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:59.050
By the late 1980s, pages were routinely sold for prices in the tens of dollars in high-volume

00:04:59.050 --> 00:04:59.530
markets.

00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:04.550
That was a reduction of roughly an order of magnitude from the earliest VHF units.

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:07.970
The idiot index of the new design was far lower.

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:13.310
The dominant expenses had shifted from custom radio engineering to commodity crystals

00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:16.670
and silicon that tracked broader semiconductor learning curves.

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:18.250
Trade-offs remained.

00:05:18.910 --> 00:05:21.330
The one-way link could not confirm message receipt.

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:24.270
Battery life depended on strict duty cycling.

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:27.970
Coverage still required a network of high-power transmitters.

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:33.890
Those limits were accepted because the service model only promised notification, not conversation.

00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:39.510
The remaining gap to the absolute material floor was now dominated by the plastic housing,

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:43.830
battery, and final test rather than by radio-specific engineering.

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:49.890
A receiver whose only job is to wake, compare and address, and display a short string reveals

00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:54.550
how many radio parts are optional once the use case is stripped to its physical minimum.

00:05:54.550 --> 00:06:00.270
Treating the protocol as shared infrastructure rather than proprietary hardware lets volume

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:03.490
drive every subsequent component toward its material cost.

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:08.870
The same logic of fixing the message format first and then minimizing the hardware that

00:06:08.870 --> 00:06:13.530
implements it appears again in modern low power wide area networks for sensors.

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:19.210
What would change if every short burst alerting device today began from the same question

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:22.510
of what the radio link must physically carry and nothing more?

00:06:22.510 --> 00:06:25.690
That's a wrap on today's first principles breakdown.

00:06:26.270 --> 00:06:28.890
The ideas travel further when you pass them on.

00:06:29.310 --> 00:06:30.710
Send this to a fellow builder.

